\section{Participants}
\label{sec:method_participants}
Twenty-eight ($N=28$) participants were recruited for the study (14 female, 14 male). To participate, individuals were required to have normal or corrected-to-normal vision and no history of neurological disorders. Three participants were excluded prior to analysis: two due to a high number of self-reported keypress errors (greater than 10) which compromised label integrity, and one due to an undisclosed neurological condition. The experimenter's own data were recorded separately for pipeline validation and were never part of the recruited sample; they are excluded from all reported results. The final sample consisted of $n=25$ participants (age range 20--30 years, $M = 24.6$, $SD = 2.9$, 13 female, 12 male). Figure~\ref{fig:participant_inclusion} traces this selection from the recorded sessions through to the analysed sample. It also accounts for the participant-ID range used throughout this thesis: the first three recorded sessions (P1--P3) were pilot recordings made for pipeline validation and were never part of the recruited sample, so the recruited participants carry the identifiers P4--P31, and the retained identifiers still run up to P31 even though only $n=25$ participants remain.

