\subsection{Band Power and Statistical Moments}
Following window extraction, a comprehensive feature set was computed for each valid temporal window (executed via \url{https://github.com/coffeeandcoffee/eeg_tiktok_pipeline/data_analysis/step05_feature_engineering.py}). Two distinct extraction schemes are applied. For each of the seven frequency bands at each of the four electrodes, the mean and standard deviation of the normalized envelope are computed, alongside the relative power, Hjorth, and peak/macro frequency features described in the following subsections. Minimum and maximum were computed during development but are excluded from the final feature set. The undecomposed raw broadband signal is treated separately and is described at the end of this section. An example of the extracted statistics for one 1-second window of one frequency band (alpha) at one electrode of one participant is depicted in Figure~\ref{fig:stat_moments}.

In addition to these four moments, a Relative Power feature was computed for each band and electrode as the mean power of that band divided by the summed mean power across all bands at the same electrode. This expresses each band's contribution as a proportion of the total spectral power measured at that electrode and is therefore invariant to overall amplitude scaling.

